<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">1. INTRODUCTION</h2>
            <p>This document provides basic instruction for the installation and commissioning of the <span data-field="instrument_type">{{ instrument_type }}</span>. This transmitter is connected to a process by means of impulse lines and can measure Pressure or Absolute pressure. The measurement is transmitted to a control system by means of a 4-20 mA signal or a digital signal (HART) or by means of a digital signal indicated by means of one of the (optional) local or remote displays.</p>
            <p>Instructions for preliminary checks, proper transmitter location, installation, wiring, power-up and zero calibration (trimming) of the transmitter are listed in the following.</p>
            <p>In order to assure operation and plant safety it is essential that the installation is carried out by personnel suitably trained on the local applicable codes on hazardous location, electrical and instrumentation principles. Please read these instructions carefully before installing the transmitter. The protection provided by the equipment may be impaired if the equipment is used in a manner not specified.</p>
            <p>For more information refer to the reference manual (document <span data-field="reference_doc_number">{{ reference_doc_number }}</span>) available at <span data-field="reference_url">{{ reference_url }}</span> searching for the keyword "268H" or from local ABB representatives.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: center;">
            <!-- Placeholder for Figure 1 -->
            <img src="placeholder_fig1.png" alt="Figure 1 - Product identification" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Fig. 1 - Product identification</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14pt;">2. PHASE 1 - PRELIMINARY CHECKS</h3>
        <p>Before mounting the transmitter, check the compatibility with the following measurement and safety requirements:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Explosion protection</li>
            <li>Pressure rating</li>
            <li>Operating voltage limits</li>
            <li>Process and ambient temperature limits</li>
            <li>Environmental limits</li>
            <li>Corrosion</li>
        </ul>

        <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-top: 20px;">
            <div style="flex: 1;">
                <div class="warning">
                    <strong>Warning !</strong> - For potentially explosive atmosphere applications see the temperature range specified in the certificate/approval relevant to the intended type of use.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="flex: 1;">
                <div class="caution">
                    <strong>Note</strong> - The transmitter may be used as a safety accessory (as defined by the Pressure Equipment Directive 97/23/EC) as part of a shutdown system. In this case, the transmitter must be correctly rated and safe mode for the 4-20 mA signal (as per NAMUR NE43).
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p>Explosions could result in death or serious injury. Installation of this transmitter in a Hazardous Area (i.e. a potentially explosive atmosphere) must be in accordance with the applicable national, international and international standards, codes, regulations and directives.</p>
            <p>Please review the approvals and marking of the transmitter shown on the label attached to the transmitter (see figure 1 Ref. C). Note that this is a sample, read the values on the real label attached to the transmitter. It is necessary to check for installation in Hazardous Areas. It is necessary to check</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <h4 style="font-size: 12pt;">2.2 Pressure and Temperature Limits</h4>
            <p>The maximum allowable pressure (PS) and maximum/minimum allowable temperature (TS) of the pressure transmitter, for the European market are indicated on the tag plate (ref. D) of Figure 1. In the use please refer to the instrument data sheets details for the specific transmitter. For the US market, please refer to the data sheet or from local ABB representatives.</p>
            <div class="caution">
                <strong>Warning !</strong> - For potentially explosive atmosphere applications see the temperature range specified in the certificate/approval relevant to the intended type of use.
            </div>
            <p>For pressure transmitter with ATEX combined approval, before installation, the transmitter should be permanently marked with the intended Protection Concept (e.g. intrinsically safe, explosion proof) on the safety label. The transmitter can be used only in accordance with this Protection Concept for its whole life.</p>
            <p>In order to assure operation and plant safety it is essential that the installation is carried out by personnel suitably trained on the local applicable codes on hazardous location, electrical and instrumentation principles. Please read these instructions carefully before installing the transmitter. The protection provided by the equipment may be impaired if the equipment is used in a manner not specified.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <h4 style="font-size: 12pt;">PS values</h4>
        <p>Models 268H, 268NS</p>
        <p>- 14MPa, 140bar, 203psi for sensors Code E, G, H, M</p>
        <p>- 21MPa, 210bar, 304psi for sensors Code P, Q, S</p>

        <h4 style="font-size: 12pt;">Proof pressure</h4>
        <p>The transmitter can be exposed without leaking to line pressure during the proof test.</p>
        <p>Models 268H, 268NS</p>
        <p>- 28MPa, 280bar, 406psi for sensors Code E, G, H, M</p>
        <p>- 40MPa, 400bar, 580psi for sensors Code P, Q, S</p>
        <p><sup>1</sup> Sensor code is the 6th character of the product code on label Ref. A.</p>
        <p>Meet ANSI/ISA-S 82.03 hydrostatic test requirements and SAMPA PMC 27.1.</p>
        <p>Other 268H and 268NS models using direct mount and/or remote seal(s) are compliant to SEP (Sound Engineering Practice).</p>
    </div>

