<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">2.4 ENVIRONMENTAL LIMITS</h2>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.1 Electromagnetic compatibility (EMC)</h4>
            <p>In accordance with EN 50081-1 for emission and EN 50082-2 for immunity requirements and test.</p>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.2 Humidity</h4>
            <p>Relative humidity: up to 100% annual average</p>
            <p>Condensing, icing: admissible</p>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.3 Vibration resistance</h4>
            <p>Accelerations up to 2g at frequencies up to 1000Hz (according to IEC 60068-2-6).</p>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.4 Shock resistance</h4>
            <p>Acceleration: 50g</p>
            <p>Duration: 11ms (according to IEC 60068-2-27).</p>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.5 Wet and dust-laden atmospheres</h4>
            <p>The transmitter is dust and sand tight and protected against immersion effects as defined by IEC EN 60529 (1989) to IP 67 (or equivalent). The transmitter is suitable for use in hazardous areas.</p>
            <h4 style="font-size: 14pt;">2.4.6 Fill fluid warning</h4>
            <p>Be sure that the fill fluid (indicated on label Ref. B) can mix safely with the process fluid in case of rupture of the sensor membrane.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">2.5 CORROSION</h2>
            <p>Be sure that the process fluid is compatible with the material of the process flanges and sensor diaphragm.</p>
            <p>The process fluid compatibility table is available at <span data-field="compatibility_url">{{ compatibility_url }}</span> (inserting in the "search tool" the keyword "TBCOR") or from local ABB representatives.</p>
            <div class="caution">
                <strong>Note</strong> - Data of the table are based on information from manufacturers.
            </div>
            <p>Since corrosion involves many more variables than air and temperature, the transmitter is not guaranteed to be corrosion proof, and pitting, the table should be used only as a reference in the absence of other information. The transmitter is not guaranteed to be corrosion proof. If a particular material is best suited, please contact our local ABB representatives.</p>
            <div class="warning">
                <strong>Warning !</strong> - For safety purpose the design corrosion allowance of the transmitter is not guaranteed. The transmitter is not guaranteed to be corrosion proof. If the process fluid is corrosive, the transmitter must be protected by a suitable material according to the applicable standards. Please contact our local ABB representatives.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">2.6 SPECIAL SERVICES</h2>
        <p>In case of Oxygen or Hydrogen or other special services, the transmitter has to be handled with a special care in order to prevent contamination with impure substances. It is necessary to use "sterile" gloves and that the removal of protection bags must be done immediately before the installation. Do not flush with impure fluids.</p>
    </div>

